    "created_at": "2026-05-31T00:08:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-31T00:08:13Z",
    "body": "Cross-post from plumbline reproduction work (2026-05-30):\n\n- Native DIODE val + `lstsq` scale-and-shift (771, ViT-L): AbsRel **~0.21** vs paper Table 2 **0.066**.\n- Indoor split alone: **~0.072** (matches paper); outdoor native **~0.33** drives the gap.\n- MoGe HF bundle eval (1024\u00d7768 warp, disparity-affine-invariant + clamp): **~0.05** \u2014 closer but still ~15\u201318% under 0.066.\n\nThe DA-V2 repo has no zero-shot DIODE eval script. Closest public recipe we found is MoGe `eval_baseline.py` + `Ruicheng/monocular-geometry-evaluation`.\n\nDocs: https://github.com/kmatzen/plumbline/blob/main/docs/DA_V2_TABLE2_UPSTREAM_EVAL.md and https://github.com/kmatzen/plumbline/blob/main/docs/D29_DIODE_TABLE2_HANDOFF.md\n\nWere Table 2 DIODE numbers computed on a MoGe-style bundle, indoor-only, or a different outdoor treatment?",
